(cid:129) device tracking requirements; and
(cid:129) other post-market surveillance requirements, which apply when necessary to protect the public health or to provide
additional safety and effectiveness data for the device.
Failure to comply with applicable regulatory requirements can result in enforcement action by the FDA, which may include any
of the following:
(cid:129) warning letters and untitled letters;
(cid:129) fines, injunctions, consent decrees, and civil penalties;
(cid:129) recalls, withdrawals, administrative detention, or seizure of products;
(cid:129) operating restrictions, partial suspension or total shutdown of production;
(cid:129) withdrawals of 510(k) clearances or PMA approvals that have already been granted;
(cid:129) refusal to grant 510(k) clearance or PMA approvals of new products; and/or
(cid:129) criminal prosecution.
